{"ts": "2026-10-17T17:07:09.931759Z", "run_id": "r-20261017T1706Z-8d16", "unit": "openspec:add-telemetry-heavy-path-spans", "seq": 8, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-002", "target": "H-8b8cc0d1", "decision": "accept", "by": "human", "reason": "in scope. The proposal names history/ingest.py among the files this change edits, and the spec requires that work handed to thread pools in history backfill and sync runs in a fresh copy of the caller's context per task. The diff of packages/core/src/mintmory/core/history/ingest.py is exactly that: _prepare_session is wrapped in telemetry.run_in_context before it is submitted to the executor, in backfill and in sync, and nothing else changes.", "text_sha256": "ebb44d7c036de614c28f50ffa4bb1ab17867b0b0411e047f13d6242bf74d4da1", "answer_sha256": "0e3deed8ddf17ca4b3d41873b4635841bd5f347212e89ffe1153ba783c6a9391"}
{"ts": "2026-10-17T17:07:09.975344Z", "run_id": "r-20261017T1706Z-8d16", "unit": "openspec:add-telemetry-heavy-path-spans", "seq": 9, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-003", "target": "H-e0757174", "decision": "reject", "by": "human", "reason": "an independent full-diff review (51/51 unit tests and the full gate pass; with telemetry off every command matches the base) found two breaks of this spec's rule that recording a metric point or attribute SHALL never raise into the caller (spec.md line 35; tasks.md asks for try/except). (1) telemetry.counts_added (telemetry.py:1006) calls add_count outside its try, and add_count does not guard counter.add or the instrument creation: with a failing meter, storage add_memory (storage.py:468, storage_postgres.py:418) raises RuntimeError after the row is stored, so mintmory add exits non-zero and a retry stores a duplicate. (2) span() sets attributes without a guard (telemetry.py:630), so embed_span and file_span make embed() raise when set_attribute raises. WHEN the meter, a counter's add, a histogram's record or a span's set_attribute raises inside a telemetry helper (counts_added, add_count, record_value, the span attributes of embed_span and file_span) THEN the error stays inside telem", "text_sha256": "05f8056b48da5aa5cc54ef364c92680c1d874328ebcb036e699149f7544ba281", "answer_sha256": "6688fdbb584d526a8136d5116c033f7ccce8c3df7defe3b94af1159d99cda663"}
